Your current setup uses Droid's managed models. To switch to BYOM, you need to add a `models` array with your own model endpoint. Here are the common BYOM configurations:

**Option 1: OpenAI-Compatible (OpenAI, Together, Groq, etc.)**
```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "gpt-4o",
      "name": "GPT-4o",
      "provider": "openai",
      "apiKey": "$OPENAI_API_KEY",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.openai.com/v1"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Option 2: Ollama (Local Models)**
```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "llama3.1",
      "name": "Llama 3.1",
      "provider": "ollama",
      "baseUrl": "http://localhost:11434/v1"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Option 3: Anthropic (Claude)**
```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "claude-opus-4",
      "name": "Claude Opus 4",
      "provider": "anthropic",
      "apiKey": "$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1"
    }
  ]
}
```

Which model provider do you want to use? I'll need:
1. **Provider** (openai, anthropic, ollama, groq, together, etc.)
2. **Model ID** (e.g., `gpt-4o`, `claude-opus-4`, `llama3.1:8b`)
3. **API key** (if using a hosted provider) — we'll store it securely
4. **Base URL** (optional, if using a custom endpoint)

